    <!--
      The platform limitation, stated outright at the bottom of the screen.

      Anyone arriving from Windows Task Manager will look for a per-app CPU and
      memory table. It is not missing by oversight, and saying so is far more
      useful than leaving them hunting for a tab that cannot exist.
    -->
    <string name="perf_platform_note">Note: Android does not allow apps to measure the CPU or memory used by <i>other</i> apps. That access was removed in Android 8.0, so no app can show a per-app process table like Windows Task Manager. The figures above are device-wide, plus this app\'s own usage.</string>

